      steps: ['Write the input grammar, maximum size, stop rule, summary formulas, and seven expected cases before coding.', 'Create `std::vector<int> minutes`; use a while loop that stops on done or size 7, parses each line, and pushes only valid 1-300 values.', 'Print accepted position and remaining capacity after each successful push; invalid text or range prints one error and leaves vector size unchanged.', 'Use a range-based for loop to compute total, shortest, longest, and target count; calculate average as floating point only after proving nonempty.', 'Run empty, one-value, normal-three, exact-60, invalid-then-valid, capacity-seven, and early-done cases with expected and actual summaries.', 'Temporarily use `index <= minutes.size()` in a small display loop, capture the failure or out-of-range exception using `.at`, repair it to a safe range, and rerun all cases.'],
      criteria: ['The collection loop stops at done or seven accepted values and makes progress after every input.', 'Invalid and out-of-range entries never change vector size or stored values.', 'Empty input performs no division and reports the exact empty message.', 'Every nonempty summary has correct count, total, one-decimal average, minimum, maximum, and >=60 count.', 'No index equals vector size, and all seven cases are recorded.', 'The off-by-one defect is reproduced, explained, repaired, and the final build is warning-free.'],
