      outcome: 'A multi-file in-memory loan desk with three independent Equipment objects, six exact normal/failure/copy cases, and evidence for bounded exception handling, copy independence, and automatic lifetime.',
      brief: 'Create `equipment-desk/` with `main.cpp`, `equipment.cpp`, and `equipment.hpp`. Equipment owns a nonblank label, nonnegative total count, and available count. The constructor establishes total=available. `borrow_one()` and `return_one()` reject impossible transitions before mutation. Use the supplied bounded scaffold: invalid construction throws `std::invalid_argument`, invalid transitions throw `std::logic_error`, and each expected failure is caught immediately in its named case so the exact message and unchanged state can be checked. Const member functions expose label, total, available, and a status line. Store three objects in a vector. Do not use inheritance, pointers, new, delete, or a custom destructor.',
      steps: ['Copy the class interface, invariant, four exact exception contracts, supplied throw/catch syntax, six cases, and ownership questions before implementing fields.', 'Declare private label, total, and available fields; implement a constructor that throws the supplied `std::invalid_argument` messages for blank label or negative total before an object becomes usable.', 'Implement const observer methods plus borrow_one and return_one; throw the supplied `std::logic_error` messages for no-available or already-all-returned before changing available.', 'Create Camera, Projector, and Recorder values in a vector; run the normal transition case and the four named failure cases through the supplied local try/catch pattern, checking exact message and unchanged state.', 'Copy the camera into a local `practice_copy`, borrow from the copy, and record original/copy status; explain why std::string and integer fields remain independently managed.', 'Temporarily assign the constructor parameter to itself instead of the field, inspect the blank field in the debugger, repair with a member initializer list, and rerun all six cases warning-free.'],
      criteria: ['No successfully constructed Equipment has a blank label, negative total, or available outside 0..total.', 'Blank label and negative total each throw the exact documented `std::invalid_argument` before an object is stored.', 'Borrow at zero and return at total each throw the exact documented `std::logic_error` before state changes.', 'Every expected exception is caught only around its named case; unexpected exception type/message or missing exception is reported as a failed case.', 'All observers are const, fields remain private, and three vector elements retain independent state across every operation.', 'The copy probe changes only practice_copy and uses no raw allocation or manual deletion.', 'The constructor-shadowing defect is reproduced, inspected, repaired, and all six supplied cases pass.'],
      hints: ['A member initializer list constructs fields directly instead of assigning after construction.', 'Check a transition before decrementing or incrementing available.', 'The default value semantics are the point of the copy probe; do not introduce a pointer to share state.'],
      templates: [
        { label: 'equipment.hpp interface', content: '#pragma once\n\n#include <string>\n\nnamespace campus {\nclass Equipment {\npublic:\n    Equipment(std::string label, int total);\n    const std::string& label() const;\n    int total() const;\n    int available() const;\n    void borrow_one();\n    void return_one();\n    std::string status_line() const;\nprivate:\n    std::string label_;\n    int total_;\n    int available_;\n};\n}\n' },
        { label: 'Supplied nonblank helper', content: '#include <cctype>\n#include <string>\n\nnamespace campus {\nbool has_non_whitespace(const std::string& text) {\n    for (const unsigned char ch : text) {\n        if (!std::isspace(ch)) return true;\n    }\n    return false;\n}\n}\n' },
        { label: 'Constructor initializer-list skeleton', content: '#include <stdexcept>\n#include <utility>\n\nnamespace campus {\nEquipment::Equipment(std::string label, int total)\n    : label_{std::move(label)}, total_{total}, available_{total} {\n    if (!has_non_whitespace(label_)) {\n        throw std::invalid_argument{"label must not be blank"};\n    }\n    if (total_ < 0) {\n        throw std::invalid_argument{"total must not be negative"};\n    }\n}\n}\n' },
        { label: 'Invariant and errors', content: 'Invariant: label has at least one non-whitespace character; total >= 0; 0 <= available <= total.\nblank or whitespace-only label -> std::invalid_argument("label must not be blank")\nnegative total -> std::invalid_argument("total must not be negative")\nborrow at zero -> std::logic_error("no item is available")\nreturn at total -> std::logic_error("all items are already returned")\n' },
        { label: 'Six state and failure cases', content: '1. Normal independence: Camera(2), Projector(1), Recorder(3); borrow then return Camera -> 2/2, others unchanged\n2. Construct "   " label -> exact invalid_argument; no object stored\n3. Construct total -1 -> exact invalid_argument; no object stored\n4. Camera(0), borrow -> exact logic_error; remains 0/0\n5. Projector(1), return before borrow -> exact logic_error; remains 1/1\n6. Copy Camera(2), borrow copy -> original 2/2; copy 1/2\n' },
        { label: 'Lifetime note', content: '- Which object owns each label string?\n- What happens to local practice_copy at scope exit?\n- Why are new/delete unnecessary here?\n- What evidence shows the original and copy are independent?\n' },
        { label: 'Supplied bounded exception scaffold', content: '#include <stdexcept>\n\n// Inside a command, check before mutation:\nif (/* invalid-transition condition */) {\n    throw std::logic_error{"no item is available"};\n}\n\n// Around one named expected-failure case only:\ntry {\n    campus::Equipment invalid{"   ", 1};\n    // Record FAIL: the expected exception was not thrown.\n} catch (const std::invalid_argument& error) {\n    // Compare error.what() with "label must not be blank".\n} catch (...) {\n    // Record FAIL: wrong exception type.\n}\n\n// Use the same narrow pattern with std::logic_error for one transition.\n// Never wrap the complete program in catch (...), and never continue after an unexpected failure.\n' },
      ],
      stretch: 'After every case passes, add a const `can_borrow()` observer and one boundary case; do not expose a setter or raw pointer.',
      sessions: [{ title: 'Construct and protect object state', minutes: 105, stepIndexes: [1, 2, 3] }, { title: 'Prove independence, lifetime, and focused repair', minutes: 105, stepIndexes: [4, 5, 6] }],
