    proof: ['Class interface/implementation, written invariant, and supplied bounded exception pattern', 'Six-case transcript covering normal behavior and every exact invalid-construction/transition message', 'Original-versus-copy status evidence and RAII/lifetime explanation', 'Constructor-shadowing debugger evidence and repair'],
    reflections: ['Why must each constructor or transition check happen before mutation or storage?', 'What did the copy probe demonstrate about ordinary C++ value ownership?'],
